,5,6,7,8}.","statement":"It suffices to consider the five disjoint cases m=4,5,6,7,8."},{"citations":[],"depends_on":["classify-maximum"],"id":"case-eight","justification":"The remaining elements must sum to 9-8=1, and the only subset of {1,...,7} with sum 1 is {1}.","statement":"For m=8, the sole subset is {8,1}."},{"citations":[],"depends_on":["classify-maximum"],"id":"case-seven","justification":"The remaining elements must sum to 2, and the only subset of {1,...,6} with sum 2 is {2}.","statement":"For m=7, the sole subset is {7,2}."},{"citations":[],"depends_on":["classify-maximum"],"id":"case-six","justification":"The remaining elements must sum to 3. The distinct-element subsets of {1,...,5} summing to 3 are {3} and {2,1}.","statement":"For m=6, the subsets are {6,3} and {6,2,1}."},{"citations":[],"depends_on":["classify-maximum"],"id":"case-five","justification":"The remaining elements must sum to 4. The distinct-element subsets of {1,2,3,4} summing to 4 are {4} and {3,1}.","statement":"For m=5, the subsets are {5,4} and {5,3,1}."},{"citations":[],"depends_on":["classify-maximum"],"id":"case-four","justification":"The remaining elements must sum to 5 using only {1,2,3}. Its total is 6, so such a subset must omit elements of total 1; it therefore omits only 1 and is {2,3}.","statement":"For m=4, the sole subset is {4,3,2}."},{"citations":[],"depends_on":["case-eight","case-seven","case-six","case-five","case-four"],"id":"total-count","justification":"The five largest-element cases are disjoint and contain respectively 1, 1, 2, 2, and 1 subsets. Their total is 1+1+2+2+1=8.","statement":"The exhaustive list contains eight subsets."}],"question_status":"answered","tool_requests":[]}
